 ## Downstream Contract Work
 
-After selection, define the submission envelope, current-state response, unresolved-work representation, and resolution operation here. Tablet-sync will size its local storage and retry state machine around that envelope. Review-export will size its coordinator interface and export eligibility rules around the unresolved-work representation. Both must link back to this node rather than invent their own concurrency semantics.
+Tablet-sync and review-export are separate segments and are designed after this node. The obligations this design creates for them:
+
+- Tablet-sync stores the `base_revision_id` of every visit it fetches or submits, retries on the idempotency key, and shows the worker when a submitted visit is awaiting coordinator resolution. It must handle the validation rejections named above, including re-fetch after a lost base revision.
+- Review-export reads the unresolved flag and competing tips to drive a revision comparison view, calls the resolution operation with the tip set it displayed, handles the stale-tip-set rejection, and decides export eligibility from resolution state.
+
+Both link back to this node for concurrency semantics rather than defining their own.
